    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW21DH7fdHNhSnfhtpK1ep4if)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Order: independent of #410 (already merged); branch is `489-…`, based on `main`.\n- Depends on: nothing open.\n- If merged out of order: doc conflicts expected with #487 (`sp-batch-report.org`, `sp-org-lint.org`) and with the DEVONthink PRs (#420, #421, #443, #451, #452, #455) on lines that say `C-c k d`; keep their text and change the key to `C-; k d`. Their `keymap-set sp-devonthink-map` lines still work (the map is mounted at `C-; k d`).\n- After merging: none.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Request:** `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-keys` (PR #410) had no usable key; simplify the academic keymaps; unify the lint keymaps; then remove the shims. #410 is merged, so this is a new PR.\n- **Cause of the missing key:** `C-c w b k` was bound twice: `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-keys` globally and `citar-vulpea-add-reference` in `org-mode-map`. In an Org note the key added a citekey, so the fix looked unbound. (The command is `-fix-keys`, there is no `-fix-key`.)\n- **Three leader groups** in `sp-keys` (leader `C-;`):\n  - `B` bibliography, from `C-c w b`;\n  - `k` knowledge search, from `C-c k`;\n  - `L` lint, new: one sub-letter per module, the same verbs everywhere: `l` list (dry run), `a` apply (convert), `r` restore.\n- **Reports:** the footnote report applied with `a`; it is now `A` like every other report. Rule written in `sp-batch-report.org`: lower-case acts on the entry at point, upper-case on the whole list.\n- **No shims for the moved keys** (removed on request): the old `C-c w b …`, `C-c k …` and footnote `a` are unbound. The older shims in `sp-keys-moved` (easysession, `C-c e b b`) are untouched.\n- Docs are bullet lists (`sp-keys.org`, `sp-academic.org`, `sp-batch-report.org`, `sp-org-lint.org`, the design doc status); `.el` files tangled from them. No CHANGELOG edit, `when-let*` only, GUI-only keys, no `C-z`/`C-x`/`C-c`/`C-v` root.\n- Left alone: `C-c w` keys outside `b` (reading, olivetti, elfeed, collection query, Denote), `n b`, and `sp-org-normalise`/`sp-vulpea-meta-order` lints (no key before, none now).\n\n## Old to new keys\n\n| Old (now unbound) | New |\n|---|---|\n| `C-c w b r` register | `C-; B r` |\n| `C-c w b o` / `e` / `n` / `c` citar open / entry / notes / create | `C-; B o` / `e` / `n` / `c` |\n| `C-c w b d` / `k` / `K` (Org only) | `C-; B d` / `k` / `K` (now global) |\n| `C-c w b b` / `i` / `u` / `s` / `a` fetch | `C-; B b` / `i` / `u` / `s` / `a` |\n| `C-c w b l` / `L` lint report / convert | `C-; L b l` / `C-; L b a` |\n| `C-c w b k` (key fix, shadowed) | `C-; L b f k` |\n| `C-c k l` `I` `s` `S` `.` `R` `t` `T` | `C-; k l` `I` `s` `S` `.` `R` `t` `T` |\n| `C-c k d …` DEVONthink map | `C-; k d …` |\n| footnote report `a` | `A` |\n\nNew `L` groups (`l` list, `a` apply unless noted):\n\n| Keys | Command pair |\n|---|---|\n| `L b` | BibTeX `sp-bibtex-lint-dryrun` / `-convert`; `r` restore dropped |\n| `L b f` + `n` `c` `C` `f` `i` `k` `o` `p` | fix authors, crossref (`C` its report), files, indent, keys, order, prefixes |\n| `L m` | litnote metadata fill (`sp-litnotes-meta-fill-all-*`) |\n| `L q` | litnote titles in quotes (`sp-litnotes-meta-title-lint-*`) |\n| `L t` / `L r` | litnote titles, authors and year / litnote references |\n| `L f` | footnotes |\n| `L g` | tags: `l` `sp-org-tag-lint`, `b` current buffer |\n| `L u`, `L u w` | author notes, their Works tables |\n| `L n` | notes filing; `r` restore, `s` schedule |\n\n## Tested\n\n- New `tests/sp-keys-test.el`: 4 pass (Emacs 29.3 batch): each lint group is `-dryrun` on `l` and `-convert` on `a`, the key fix is `C-; L b f k`, the old academic keys are not in the shim table.\n- Still pass: `sp-batch-report-test` 21, `sp-org-lint-test` 17, `sp-org-tag-lint-test` 13, `sp-author-notes-bibtex-test` 16.\n- Not run: a real Emacs with the full config, the GUI, Alfred or the real vault.\n- Not done: which-key labels are untested (`which-key-add-keymap-based-replacements`).\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Pull this branch, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`) (untested by Claude)\n- [x] `C-; ` then `C-h`: which-key lists `B`, `k`, `L` with names (untested by Claude)\n- [x] `C-; L` then `C-h`: lists `b m q t r f g u n`; `C-; L b f` lists the seven fixes\n- [ ] On a scratch `.bib`: `C-; L b l` shows the lint report, `C-; L b f k` runs the key fix, `C-; L b a` asks which fixes to run\n- [ ] In an Org note and in a `.bib` buffer: `C-; B k` / `K` add and remove a citekey of the note (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Per module, `l` shows a dry run and writes nothing: `C-; L m l`, `L q l`, `L t l`, `L r l`, `L f l`, `L g l`, `L u l`, `L u w l`, `L n l`\n- [ ] `a` applies after a question: `C-; L f a` on a scratch vault (backup made)\n- [x] `C-; B b` `i` `u` `s` `a` start the fetch commands; `C-; B o` opens citar\n- [ ] `C-; k l` litdb, `k s` semantic, `k t` tab p-search; `C-; k d` then `o` opens a record\n- [ ] Edge: footnote report `A` applies and `a` does nothing; tag report `a` still registers the tag at point\n- [x] Old keys are unbound: `C-c w b l`, `C-c w b k`, `C-c k s`, `C-c k d` say \"undefined\"\n- [x] `M-x sp-keys-audit`: no void command among the new groups\n- [ ] Regression: `C-; b b`, `C-; g s`, `C-; E a` (embark), `C-c a`, `C-c c`, and the old easysession shim `C-c s s` still work\n- [ ] Keys reach Emacs on the Mac with Alfred running (`C-;` then `L`) (untested by Claude)\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (`git clean -fd` only after `git clean -nd`).\n- Return to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main` and `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally delete the test branch: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D 489-academic-lint-keymaps`.\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n- Apply keys (`a`) write to the vault or `.bib`: restore from the backup folder the command reported, or `git -C ~/notes restore .`.\n- Fish shell works for all of the above; no yadm steps.\n\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCzaeJZR142mh9L4AR\n",
